==========================================================================
NOAA / NCEP NAM
==========================================================================

The NAM model source (github.com/MatthewPyle-NOAA/NAM and EricRogers-NOAA/nam_wcoss2_rocoto; the build is
pinned in build/versions.sh and the upstream commit is recorded by the build manifest) is the work of employees of
the US Government at NOAA/NCEP/EMC and is distributed without a licence file. Works of US Government employees
are in the public domain in the United States. This repository does not contain that source: the build scripts
fetch it, and our patches (build/patches/) are applied to it. A few static input files that NCEP no longer hosts
were recovered from public web-archive captures; they are US Government data.

NOAA data used as model inputs and for verification (NOAA Open Data Dissemination) is used as distributed.
FrankenNAM output keeps the operational NAM's file names so that existing tools work unchanged; the files are
labelled as FrankenNAM in the products README and on every public page.

==========================================================================
RRTMG radiation (Atmospheric and Environmental Research, Inc.)
==========================================================================

The NAM source tree includes NCEP's copy of AER's RRTMG longwave and shortwave radiation code and its
k-distribution tables (Mlawer, Iacono, Clough and co-authors). AER distributes RRTMG under the BSD 3-Clause
licence. We compile that code as part of the model and do not redistribute it from this repository. Anyone who
redistributes the built model, or the source, must keep AER's copyright notice, the licence conditions and the
disclaimer that accompany those files. AER and its contributors are not endorsing FrankenNAM.

==========================================================================
NCEPLIBS and the NAM's library stack
==========================================================================

The model and post-processing link to NCEP libraries built from their public releases (versions in
build/versions.sh): bacio, sp, ip, w3nco, w3emc, g2, g2c, g2tmpl, sigio, sfcio, gfsio, nemsio, NCEPLIBS-bufr,
CRTM, wrf_io, landsfcutil, together with zlib, libpng, jasper, HDF5 and netCDF. These are separately licensed by
their authors. Several NCEPLIBS repositories carry the GNU LGPL-3.0 and others a permissive or public-domain
terms; this repository does not contain or relicense any of them, and a built binary that links them
statically should be checked against each licence before it is distributed.
[VERIFY] the licence of each library at the pinned version before anything built is redistributed.

==========================================================================
ESMF
==========================================================================

The model runs under the Earth System Modeling Framework, version 7.1.0r, built from its release source with the
patches in build/patches/esmf-*.patch. ESMF is licensed under the University of Illinois/NCSA Open Source
License. Our patches to ESMF are provided under that same licence, and its copyright notice and licence text
must accompany any redistribution of ESMF or a binary containing it.

==========================================================================
UPP, wgrib2
==========================================================================

The post-processor (UPP) is built from the tree the NAM uses, with the patches in build/patches/uppgnu-*.patch,
and keeps the licence terms of that tree. wgrib2 (NOAA/NCEP/CPC, Wesley Ebisuzaki) is installed on the runner and
used to write the final grid-218 files; it is distributed under its own licence (GPL-2.0 terms, with a bundled
iplib), and we call it as a separate program and do not redistribute it. [VERIFY] both licences before the
runner image or any binary is shared.

==========================================================================
WRF-derived tables
==========================================================================

Vtable.SEED and METGRID.TBL.seed are adapted from the NAM's own Vtable and from WPS tables, which come from the
WRF/WPS distribution under its public-domain statement (NCAR/UCAR). Original lines are marked in the files.

==========================================================================
Python packages, base map
==========================================================================

site/ and verify/ use numpy, scipy, matplotlib, pyproj, Pillow and ecCodes (BSD or Apache-2.0 or similar
licences; ecCodes is Apache-2.0), installed from PyPI and not copied here. The base map in site/render/base/
is derived from Natural Earth, which is in the public domain.

